# I010 – Sharing of Member Personal Information

| Field | Details |
|-------|---------|
| **Incident ID** | I010 |
| **Date** | 2025 |
| **Perpetrator** | [Undex](../people/undex) |
| **Severity** | 🔴 Critical |
| **Status** | Confirmed |

---

## Summary

Undex compiled personal information about two Federal Gamers members — sourced through a combination of information shared in confidence in private channels, cross-referencing social media accounts, and information obtained via the fake bot incident (I007) — and threatened to release it publicly unless Joshua Baloni agreed to reinstate Undex's mod role and drop all pending sanctions.

The information included real first names, general geographic locations, and in one case a school name.

---

## Timeline

| Time | Event |
|------|-------|
| Day 1 | Undex DMs Joshua with a "file" claiming to contain personal info on two members |
| Day 1 | Undex demands reinstatement of mod role and removal of all sanctions within 24 hours |
| Day 1 | Joshua does not comply; escalates to full leadership |
| Day 2 | Undex posts a partial sample in a mutual server as a show of intent |
| Day 2 | Affected members notified and advised |
| Day 3 | Undex permanently blacklisted; matter reported to Discord Trust & Safety |

---

## Impact

- Two members had personal information exposed to a limited audience
- Both affected members reported significant distress
- One member temporarily deactivated their Discord account

---

## Response

Permanent blacklist applied. Undex's account reported to Discord. Affected members were supported directly by leadership. All channels Undex had access to were audited for further data exposure.
